### Sweep B — "archaeological interventions" (4 occurrences)

- §1.1 ¶1 — was: "the materials resulting from the archaeological interventions" → now: "…from the archaeological excavations". Why: ES "los materiales resultantes de las intervenciones arqueológicas" refers to the physical yields of digs, not the administrative category.
- §1.1 ¶9 — was: "the extent and intensity of the archaeological interventions practised" → now: "…of the archaeological excavations carried out". Why: ES "practicadas" = carried out; the sentence measures fieldwork scale.
- §1.1 ¶10 — was: "recent archaeological interventions conducted with adequate methodological criteria" → now: "recent archaeological excavations conducted with…". Why: ES "intervenciones arqueológicas recientes y desarrolladas con unos criterios metodológicos adecuados" describes actual digs.
- fn 14 — KEPT literal: "an entity that took control of the archaeological interventions". Why: here intervención is the heritage-administration umbrella term — the Comisaría General de Excavaciones Arqueológicas assumed statutory control over every authorised field action (surveys as well as digs) in a legal/administrative passage; "excavations" would narrow the ES meaning. (The fnref-ch1-14 tooltip is truncated at "…took control of the arch…" and needed no edit.)

